PRSL-AI may automate actions, but the architecture must preserve appropriate human control and authorization.


---

# 26. EXCEPTION MANAGEMENT

Exceptions are permitted when justified.

However, an exception must be explicit.

Canonical Exception Record:

Exception ID
Reason
Scope
Owner
Affected Principle
Risk
Mitigation
Start Date
Expiration Date
Review Date
Status


An exception must never silently become a permanent architectural rule.

Core principle:

> Every exception must have an owner.


---

# 27. TEMPORARY DECISIONS

Temporary decisions must have:

- Explicit temporary status
- Owner
- Reason
- Review date
- Exit criteria

The word "temporary" alone is not sufficient.

A temporary decision without a review mechanism becomes technical debt.


